{"name":"Bio-Oil","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["Bio-Oil is a branded skincare oil used on scars, stretch marks and uneven tone, with the aim of making these areas look softer and smoother.","Its moisturizing oils soften the skin surface. Product-specific trials were not found, and a Cochrane review summarized on Wikipedia found no evidence that creams or oils prevent or reduce stretch marks in pregnancy."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["People massage it into the area once or twice daily as part of a routine, usually for months, and it is often paired with sun protection on scars."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["It is a cosmetic, not a drug, so it is not subject to drug approval. No safety data were found in the sources reviewed, and individual skin reactions to any topical product are possible."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Creating_bio-oil_from_solid_waste.jpg/960px-Creating_bio-oil_from_solid_waste.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f8/Creating_bio-oil_from_solid_waste.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Creating bio-oil from solid waste","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"OLUWAFEMI's","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Creating_bio-oil_from_solid_waste.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/Oil_and_water_is_the_right_mix_for_better_chem-bio_detection_141016-A-AB123-001.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/Oil_and_water_is_the_right_mix_for_better_chem-bio_detection_141016-A-AB123-001.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Oil and water is the right mix